{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\017.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "1.3.3Relationship between HCF and LCM", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[198, 110], [1161, 81], [1164, 152], [201, 182]]}, {"text": "The HCF of 14 and 24 is 2 and their LCM is 168.", "conf": 0.869, "box": [[206, 285], [1050, 261], [1051, 307], [207, 331]]}, {"text": "If we find the product of the numbers:", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[209, 353], [892, 339], [893, 388], [210, 402]]}, {"text": "14×24=336", "conf": 0.794, "box": [[459, 423], [707, 417], [708, 457], [460, 463]]}, {"text": "Now we find the product of the HCF and LCM:", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[213, 495], [1040, 475], [1041, 524], [214, 543]]}, {"text": "HCF× LCM = 2×168= 336", "conf": 0.81, "box": [[460, 564], [952, 552], [953, 590], [461, 603]]}, {"text": "From this we find that the product of 14 and 24 is equal to the product of their LCM and HCF.", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[208, 626], [1874, 593], [1875, 655], [209, 688]]}, {"text": "We can say that the product of two numbers is equal to the product of their HCF and LCM.", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[213, 703], [1831, 670], [1832, 722], [214, 755]]}, {"text": "Product of the two numbers = Product of their HCF and LCM", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[338, 773], [1424, 752], [1425, 796], [339, 818]]}, {"text": "In general if we represent the two numbers by\"a\" and \"b\".", "conf": 0.872, "box": [[215, 846], [1257, 827], [1258, 873], [216, 891]]}, {"text": "Then we canrepresent formula as:", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[215, 916], [837, 905], [838, 951], [216, 963]]}, {"text": "a× b = HCF × LCM", "conf": 0.795, "box": [[462, 984], [803, 976], [804, 1016], [463, 1024]]}, {"text": "Thisformula is applicable ifonlytwo numbers aregiven.", "conf": 0.902, "box": [[206, 1053], [1233, 1041], [1233, 1088], [206, 1100]]}, {"text": "Example 1:", "conf": 0.848, "box": [[220, 1116], [447, 1113], [447, 1156], [220, 1160]]}, {"text": "FindtheLCMofthenumber256and128iftheirHCFis128.", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[221, 1183], [1341, 1164], [1341, 1203], [221, 1221]]}, {"text": "Solution:", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[220, 1248], [408, 1245], [409, 1286], [221, 1289]]}, {"text": "As we knowthe formula:", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[222, 1313], [696, 1307], [696, 1346], [222, 1353]]}, {"text": "QuickCheck", "conf": 0.821, "box": [[1368, 1318], [1594, 1313], [1595, 1353], [1369, 1358]]}, {"text": "HCF × LCM=a×b", "conf": 0.783, "box": [[356, 1384], [714, 1377], [714, 1416], [356, 1422]]}, {"text": "If LCM of two numbers is 24", "conf": 0.844, "box": [[1362, 1400], [1802, 1392], [1803, 1435], [1363, 1443]]}, {"text": "128×LCM=256×128", "conf": 0.828, "box": [[359, 1457], [795, 1448], [796, 1486], [360, 1496]]}, {"text": "andHCFis12,findthe", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[1364, 1455], [1718, 1450], [1718, 1486], [1364, 1491]]}, {"text": "productofthetwo numbers", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[1366, 1509], [1806, 1498], [1807, 1534], [1367, 1545]]}, {"text": "256 ×128", "conf": 0.756, "box": [[612, 1526], [799, 1522], [800, 1563], [613, 1567]]}, {"text": "LCM", "conf": 0.721, "box": [[459, 1558], [561, 1555], [562, 1593], [460, 1595]]}, {"text": "128", "conf": 0.64, "box": [[672, 1572], [746, 1572], [746, 1613], [672, 1613]]}, {"text": "LCM =256", "conf": 0.747, "box": [[490, 1647], [698, 1642], [699, 1681], [491, 1687]]}, {"text": "Example 2:", "conf": 0.807, "box": [[229, 1718], [444, 1712], [445, 1756], [230, 1762]]}, {"text": "Solution:", "conf": 0.84, "box": [[230, 1849], [409, 1844], [410, 1885], [231, 1890]]}, {"text": "Asweknowtheformula:", "conf": 0.874, "box": [[233, 1915], [680, 1903], [681, 1943], [234, 1954]]}, {"text": "HCF×LCM=a×b", "conf": 0.785, "box": [[369, 1997], [722, 1989], [723, 2026], [370, 2034]]}, {"text": "16×80=a×b", "conf": 0.75, "box": [[371, 2069], [657, 2059], [658, 2098], [372, 2108]]}, {"text": "1280 =ab", "conf": 0.787, "box": [[475, 2128], [667, 2124], [668, 2165], [476, 2169]]}, {"text": "15", "conf": 0.519, "box": [[1044, 2423], [1101, 2423], [1101, 2467], [1044, 2467]]}, {"text":